      'summary' => 'Help brighten the holidays for children in need by donating a new, unwrapped toy.',
      'body' => '<p>The season of giving begins! Drop off new, unwrapped toys at the Holiday Toy Drive Kickoff at the Community Center. All toys collected go directly to children served by local family assistance programs. Suggested items include age-labeled toys for newborns through age 15. Monetary donations accepted and used to purchase specific high-need items. Hot cocoa and holiday cookies provided for all donors. Toy collection continues through December 20th at multiple drop-off locations across town.</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'Holiday Tree Lighting Ceremony',
      'date' => '2026-12-06',
      'time' => '17:00',
      'summary' => 'Gather downtown for the annual holiday tree lighting, caroling, and hot drinks.',
      'body' => '<p>Kick off the holiday season at the annual Holiday Tree Lighting in the town square! Local choirs perform caroling favorites from 5 PM, followed by remarks from the mayor and the ceremonial lighting of the community tree at 5:30 PM. Warm up with complimentary hot cocoa and cider provided by local businesses. Photos with the decorated tree encouraged. A magical evening for families, friends, and neighbors to start the season together.</p>',
    ),

    // Dec 19 — single event.
    array(
      'title' => 'Winter Solstice Lantern Walk',
      'date' => '2026-12-19',
      'time' => '17:30',
      'summary' => 'A magical lantern-lit walk through the park to celebrate the longest night of the year.',
      'body' => '<p>Mark the darkest day of the year with light, community, and a touch of magic. The Winter Solstice Lantern Walk winds through Riverside Park as participants carry handcrafted lanterns along a candlelit path. Lantern-making workshops are held beforehand (2–4 PM; materials provided). The walk begins at 5:30 PM and ends at the pavilion with mulled cider, caroling, and a community bonfire. A reflective, joyful tradition for all ages. Free to attend; suggested $5 donation for the lantern workshop.</p>',
    ),

    // Dec 31 — two events.
    array(
      'title' => "New Year's Eve Community Countdown",
      'date' => '2026-12-31',
      'time' => '21:00',
      'summary' => 'Ring in the new year together with a midnight countdown, live music, and fireworks.',
      'body' => '<p>Join your community for a safe and festive New Year\'s Eve Countdown in Central Park! Live music from local bands plays from 9 PM, with food vendors, a photo booth, and family activities running throughout the evening. A family-friendly countdown at 10 PM is followed by the midnight celebration with a ball drop, fireworks, and champagne toast for adults. All ages welcome. Free admission. Dress warmly — the party goes on rain, snow, or shine!</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'First Night Gallery Walk',
      'date' => '2026-12-31',
      'time' => '17:00',
      'summary' => 'Ring out the year with an evening stroll through downtown galleries and art spaces.',
      'body' => '<p>Before the midnight festivities, spend New Year\'s Eve exploring the arts. First Night Gallery Walk opens participating downtown galleries, studios, and art spaces from 5 to 9 PM for a free self-guided evening of art, live performance, and community. Many venues will host special year-in-review exhibitions and live music by local musicians. Pick up a map at any participating location. A civilized and beautiful way to close out the year before the countdown begins.</p>',
    ),

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // January 2027
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    // Jan 8 — two events.
    array(
      'title' => 'New Year Community Vision Session',
      'date' => '2027-01-08',
      'time' => '18:00',
      'summary' => 'Share your hopes and ideas for the new year at this open community visioning session.',
      'body' => '<p>A new year brings new possibilities. Join your neighbors for an informal evening of conversation and collective visioning. What would you love to see happen in our community this year? What challenges do we need to tackle together? Facilitated by community leaders, this open session gathers ideas that help shape our programming, advocacy, and priorities. All perspectives are welcome. Light refreshments provided. Child care available upon request (RSVP required for child care).</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'Winter Wellness Workshop',
      'date' => '2027-01-08',
      'time' => '10:00',
      'summary' => 'Beat the winter blues with practical strategies for physical and mental wellness.',
      'body' => '<p>January can be a challenging month for body and mind. The Winter Wellness Workshop brings together local health professionals to share accessible, evidence-based strategies for staying well through the cold months. Sessions cover sleep hygiene, winter nutrition, indoor movement routines, social connection, and managing seasonal mood changes. Handouts, a resource list, and a light healthy snack provided. Free to attend; registration appreciated so we can plan seating.</p>',
    ),

    // Jan 20 — two events.
    array(
      'title' => 'Martin Luther King Jr. Day of Service',
      'date' => '2027-01-20',
      'time' => '09:00',
      'summary' => 'Honor Dr. King\'s legacy with a day of community service projects across the city.',
      'body' => '<p>On this national day of remembrance and service, our community comes together to honor Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.\'s legacy through action. Volunteer teams work on projects throughout the day including housing repair assistance for elderly residents, food pantry restocking, mural painting at a community center, and literacy tutoring at the public library. All skill levels welcome. Breakfast provided at check-in. Service hours certified. Register online to select your preferred project site.</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'Civil Rights Photography Exhibition Opening',
      'date' => '2027-01-20',
      'time' => '14:00',
      'summary' => 'Opening reception for a new photography exhibition documenting the local civil rights movement.',
      'body' => '<p>The Riverside Public Library opens a new photography exhibition tracing the history of the civil rights movement in our own community. Drawn from local archives, private collections, and historical society holdings, the images document marches, organizing meetings, sit-ins, and the everyday lives of those who fought for equality here. A brief opening program includes remarks from local historians and community elders with firsthand memories. The exhibition runs through March. Free admission.</p>',
    ),

    // Jan 30 — single event.
    array(
      'title' => 'Winter Festival & Ice Sculpture Contest',
      'date' => '2027-01-30',
      'time' => '11:00',
      'summary' => 'Watch professional ice sculptors at work and enjoy winter activities in the town square.',
      'body' => '<p>Embrace the cold with our annual Winter Festival! Professional and amateur ice sculptors compete in the town square throughout the day as spectators watch stunning creations take shape from raw blocks of ice. Other activities include a chili cook-off, horse-drawn carriage rides, outdoor fire pits with s\'mores, a winter scavenger hunt for kids, and live music on the outdoor stage. Warming tents with hot drinks are stationed throughout the event area. Free admission; food available for purchase.</p>',
    ),

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // February 2027
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    // Feb 7 — two events.
    array(
      'title' => "Valentine's Day Charity Auction",
      'date' => '2027-02-07',
      'time' => '17:00',
      'summary' => 'Bid on art, experiences, and unique packages — all proceeds support the local food bank.',
      'body' => '<p>Love is in the air — and so is generosity! The Valentine\'s Day Charity Auction raises funds for the Riverside Food Bank through a lively evening of live and silent auction bidding. Items include original artwork donated by local artists, restaurant and spa packages, weekend getaways, cooking classes, and much more. Enjoy wine, cheese, and chocolates while you browse and bid. Doors open at 5 PM; live auction begins at 7 PM. Tickets required for entry — available online or at the door while space allows.</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'Community Love Letter Writing Workshop',
      'date' => '2027-02-07',
      'time' => '10:00',
      'summary' => 'Write heartfelt letters to neighbors, elders, and community heroes who deserve to be appreciated.',
      'body' => '<p>Put pen to paper and let someone know they matter. The Community Love Letter Writing Workshop invites people of all ages to write letters of appreciation to neighbors living alone, veterans, nursing home residents, teachers, and others in our community who could use a kind word. Stationery, envelopes, stamps, and prompts are provided. Finished letters are delivered by community volunteers. A warm, meaningful way to celebrate the season of love. Drop in anytime between 10 AM and 1 PM.</p>',
    ),

    // Feb 21 — two events.
    array(
      'title' => 'Black History Month Celebration',
      'date' => '2027-02-21',
      'time' => '14:00',
      'summary' => 'A community celebration honoring Black history, culture, and contributions through art and storytelling.',
      'body' => '<p>Join us for a rich afternoon of celebration and reflection in honor of Black History Month. The program features spoken word performances, a community choir, a gallery of student artwork, storytelling by local elders, and a panel discussion on the history and future of the Black community in our region. A reception with culturally inspired food follows the program. The event is free and open to all. We gather to honor, learn, and build together.</p>',
    ),
    array(
      'title' => 'Genealogy & Family History Workshop',
      'date' => '2027-02-21',
      'time' => '10:00',
      'summary' => 'Learn how to research your family roots using archives, online tools, and oral history.',
      'body' => '<p>Held in conjunction with Black History Month, this workshop is open to all who want to explore their family history. Local genealogists and library staff guide participants through using census records, vital records, immigration documents, and online databases to trace their roots. Special attention is given to researching African American ancestry, including resources for tracing family histories through and before enslavement. All experience levels welcome. Bring any family documents or photos you already have. Free to attend.</p>',
    ),

  );
